# 🚀 Node.js (TypeScript) Backend Coding Standards + Security (VAPT + OWASP)

## ✅ Architecture
- Follow layered architecture (Controller → Service → Repository)
- Keep Controllers thin (no business logic)
- Business logic must be in Services
- No DB queries inside controllers
- Use dependency injection where possible
- Avoid tightly coupled code
- Separate internal/admin/worker routes clearly

## ✅ TypeScript Best Practices
- Always use strict typing (no `any`)
- Define interfaces/types for all data structures
- Use enums/constants instead of hardcoded values
- Enable strict mode in tsconfig

## ✅ Database & Queries
- Avoid N+1 queries (use joins, IN, bulk fetch)
- NEVER call DB inside loops
- Use ORM/Query Builder properly
- Use parameterized queries ONLY
- Avoid raw/dynamic SQL
- Select only required fields
- Use transactions for critical operations
- Use bulk operations instead of loops

## ✅ Async & Performance
- Use async/await
- Avoid blocking operations
- Use Promise.all with limits
- Cache frequently used data (Redis)
- Use queues (BullMQ) for heavy jobs

## ✅ Error Handling
- Centralized error handling
- No sensitive logs
- No stack traces in production
- Use custom error classes

## ✅ Validation & Security
- Validate inputs (Joi/Zod)
- Sanitize inputs
- Use ENV variables
- Fail if critical ENV missing
- Implement JWT/OAuth properly

## 🔐 VAPT Rules

### Authentication & Authorization
- All routes must be authenticated
- No public admin/debug endpoints
- Enforce RBAC
- Validate ownership (prevent IDOR)

### Sensitive Data
- No logging of tokens/passwords
- Mask sensitive fields
- No hardcoded secrets

### API Security
- Protect all state-changing APIs
- Apply rate limiting
- Secure Swagger

### Injection Prevention
- Prevent SQL/NoSQL injection
- No dynamic query building

### SSRF
- Allow only trusted domains
- Block internal IPs

### File Handling
- Validate file size/type
- Avoid memory overflow

### Misconfiguration
- No open CORS
- No default credentials
- No debug routes in production

### Cryptography
- No plaintext tokens
- Use strong secrets
- Implement token rotation

### Logging
- No public log APIs
- Log metadata only

### Dependencies
- Maintain lockfile
- Run npm audit

### Business Logic
- Protect financial workflows
- Restrict worker endpoints

## ⚡ Performance Rules
- No DB calls inside loops
- Use bulk operations
- Fix N+1 queries

